WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.391
SQL injection prevention in Python depends on keeping untrusted data out
of SQL structure and using safe database access patterns consistently.

2
00:00:08.391 --> 00:00:16.849
The core pattern is separation: developers control the command structure,
and data values flow through parameter binding or safe ORM mechanisms.

3
00:00:16.849 --> 00:00:24.012
This applies across Flask, Django, FastAPI, scripts, internal tools, APIs,
background jobs, reports, and data pipelines.

4
00:00:24.012 --> 00:00:36.496
Strong defenses use parameterized queries, safe ORM patterns, careful
dynamic SQL design, allowlisted identifiers, input validation,
authorization, least privilege, safe errors, testing, logging, and review.

5
00:00:36.496 --> 00:00:39.020
Each control answers a different question.

6
00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:41.135
Parameterization protects values.

7
00:00:41.135 --> 00:00:43.454
Allowlists protect dynamic structure.

8
00:00:43.454 --> 00:00:45.159
Validation clarifies input.

9
00:00:45.159 --> 00:00:47.274
Authorization protects resources.

10
00:00:47.274 --> 00:00:49.116
Least privilege limits damage.

11
00:00:49.116 --> 00:00:52.936
Logging and tests keep the behavior observable and maintainable.

12
00:00:52.936 --> 00:00:58.189
ORMs, frameworks, and scanners help, but they do not replace secure design
and code review.

13
00:00:58.189 --> 00:01:10.195
Developers still need to recognize when they leave a safe ORM path, when
raw SQL is introduced, when stored procedures build dynamic commands, and
when administrative tools or background jobs take shortcuts.

14
00:01:10.195 --> 00:01:17.971
The highest-risk query is often not the obvious public route; it may be a
report, import, export, or maintenance task with broad access.

15
00:01:17.971 --> 00:01:27.453
The goal is to make safe query construction routine, unsafe query
construction rare and reviewable, and database access predictable,
testable, and maintainable.

16
00:01:27.453 --> 00:01:42.120
When teams understand data flow, constrain dynamic structure, parameterize
values, enforce authorization, and review exceptions, SQL injection
prevention becomes a normal part of Python engineering rather than an
emergency cleanup after a finding.
